Knowing exactly when your prayer timeout has expired would require 
knowing game state that isn't normally exposed to the player, modulo
!oEnlightenment, sac results and the like.

Knowing exactly the earliest turn by which it is 100% certain your
prayer timeout has expired is relatively easy. (The formula is
complicated, but the upper bound is one of two constants, depending on
if you've been crowned.)

If your point is that the turn counter isn't exposed (i.e., no
turns-on-statusline option), then it gets complicated again. The
relationship between moves and turns is usually straightforward, but
attempts to track it programmatically might founder on things like
being sent to sleep or paralyzed or anything else that takes a
variable (but possibly large) number of turns.


